2026-07-10 18:21:40,648 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: The client's requirement for response times below 2 seconds is PARTIALLY COVERED by our current technology stack. Our platform's median latency is 1.3 seconds, and common single-document queries are below 2 seconds at p95. However, complex multi-source synthesis queries may reach up to 2.5 seconds at p95, which does not fully meet the requirement.

The client's requirement for integration with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records is FULLY COVERED by our current technology stack. Our platform has standard connectors and custom adapters for SIH/DPI integration, as well as a framework alignment with Ségur / Mon espace santé–DMP, and we partner with Ligeo Santé for health interoperability.

The client's requirement for support of health interoperability standards is FULLY COVERED by our current technology stack. Our platform supports health interoperability standards such as HL7 and FHIR, with a production-grade FHIR-HL7 connector for the main resources and extended resource coverage on the roadmap.

The client's requirement for API-type interfaces is FULLY COVERED by our current technology stack. Our platform has an API-first design, with documented APIs (REST + webhook) that can be embedded in existing work environments.

The client's requirement for hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent is PARTIALLY COVERED by our current technology stack. We offer a sovereign HDS tier hosted on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, but we do not have information on whether this infrastructure is equivalent to other SecNumCloud-qualified options.

The client's requirement for particular attention to dependency on non-European suppliers is PARTIALLY COVERED by our current technology stack. We offer a sovereign European open-weight model hosted by Faber IA on OuraneCloud, which reduces dependency on non-European suppliers, but we also have the option of using top-tier proprietary models accessed via API, some of which are operated by non-European providers.

The proposed architecture would involve deploying our Atelier platform on the sovereign HDS tier hosted on OuraneCloud, utilizing our standard connectors and custom adapters for SIH/DPI integration, and supporting health interoperability standards through our FHIR-HL7 connector. We would also provide API-type interfaces for easy integration with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records. To address the response time requirement, we could explore optimizing our platform's configuration or scaling up our infrastructure to ensure that complex multi-source synthesis queries can be completed within the 2-second threshold.
