We are committed to ensuring the solution meets the client's requirements for response times below 2 seconds, although our current technology stack only partially covers this requirement, with a median latency of 1.3 seconds and common single-document queries below 2 seconds at p95. However, complex multi-source synthesis queries may reach up to 2.5 seconds at p95. We will explore optimizing our platform's configuration or scaling up our infrastructure to ensure that complex multi-source synthesis queries can be completed within the 2-second threshold.

Our solution will integrate with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), supporting health interoperability standards such as HL7 and FHIR, with a production-grade FHIR-HL7 connector for the main resources and extended resource coverage on the roadmap. We will provide API-type interfaces for easy integration with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records.

We take data sovereignty seriously and will host the solution on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, such as OuraneCloud, which is a sovereign cloud that ensures data is hosted exclusively within the European Union. We will also ensure that sensitive data is protected through encryption, pseudonymisation, and strict key management practices.

